  "notes": [
    "Irregular reflexive -AR verb with an accent shift: the *u* in the stem takes a written accent (*ú*) and carries the stress in every form except nosotros/nosotras — same pattern as *continuar*, *confiar*, *desviar*, *enviar*",
    "Not a stem-vowel change in the e→ie/o→ue/e→i/u→ue sense, so no stem-change tag applies — just an orthographic stress shift",
    "Nosotros forms stay unaccented (*nos graduamos, nos graduemos*) since the stress naturally falls on the right syllable without help",
    "Affirmative imperative attaches the reflexive pronoun with a written accent to preserve stress: *gradúate, gradúese, graduémonos, gradúense* — nosotros needs the accent here specifically because attaching *-nos* shifts where stress would otherwise fall; negative imperative keeps the pronoun separate: *no te gradúes*...",
    "Past participle: *graduado* (regular; also used as a noun — *el graduado/la graduada* = the graduate)",
    "Means \"to graduate\" — *se graduó de la universidad en 2020* (he/she graduated from university in 2020)",
    "The non-reflexive form *graduar* (\"to calibrate/adjust,\" as in a dial or instrument) is a separate, less common sense: *graduar el volumen* (to adjust the volume)",
    "Related: *graduación* (graduation), *graduado/a* (graduate, graduated)"
  ],
  "sourceFile": "Verbs/g/Graduarse.md"
